          conceptEn: "When you break a contract (renamed a field, changed the meaning of a code), clients need a new version next to the old one. Two common styles: the `/v1/orders` prefix — obvious, caches well, easy to see in logs; or `Accept: application/vnd.forge.orders+json; version=1` — the same URL, the version in a header. Do not version 'just in case' on every micro-release: that doubles the support load. Do not mix both styles in one API without a rule. Internal fields can evolve without a new version if old clients ignore them.",
