          conceptEn: "Clients should ignore unknown fields (open evolution). Adding `email` next to `name` is compatible if the field is not required on old requests. Removing `name`, renaming it to `fullName`, or changing a string into an object is a break: an old client will fail. Changing the meaning of a code (409 used to mean 'duplicate', now 409 means 'blocked') is also a break, even if the number is the same. A compatibility policy lists what is safe: additive fields, new codes with docs, new optional parameters. Contract tests (Pact, schemas) catch a break before production.",
